    {"1932", "James Chadwick, England", "The neutron", "The nucleus was heavier than its protons alone could explain. Chadwick found the missing piece: a particle with no charge. Nuclei are protons plus neutrons, which is why the same element can have different isotopes.",
     "<circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"24\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d24a4a\"/><circle cx=\"33\" cy=\"26\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8f98ab\"/><circle cx=\"27\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8f98ab\"/><circle cx=\"35\" cy=\"36\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d24a4a\" opacity=\".92\"/>",
