    {"1932", "Carl Anderson, USA", "Antimatter", "Anderson photographed a particle just like the electron, but with a positive charge: the positron. Every particle has an antiparticle, and when the two meet they vanish into light. Paul Dirac had predicted this on paper four years earlier.",
     "<circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"28\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2a5db0\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"33\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#fff\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">−</text><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"28\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#d24a4a\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"33\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#fff\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">+</text>",
