    {"2002–2016", "Scientists at Dubna, Russia and the USA", "Oganesson: the last element", "Element 118 was first made in 2002. Only three or four atoms have ever been detected, and each one lasts less than a millisecond (about 0.7 ms) before it falls apart. It was named in 2016 after the physicist Yuri Oganessian, one of only two people to have an element named after them while alive. It is the last element in this lab.",
